0s and 90s being revived for  today's market it seems crazy that the  thundercats has been left untapped for  so many years while it seems unlikely  that a theatrical live-action  thundercats movie will be released  anytime soon one actress might have  expressed interest in playing the series  leading female feline a quote attributed  to resident evil movie star miliabovic  expressing interest in playing chitara  has been republished on numerous  websites she allegedly said i've always  loved thundercats i heard they were  making a movie and then they weren't  making a movie and i'm probably getting  way too old to play catra no chitara  that's the one yovovich supposedly said  this back in 2017 but sadly not much has  changed about the status of the on-again  off-again thundercats movie  parents naming their children in honor  of their favorite fantasy franchises  isn't exactly a new phenomenon after all  there are plenty of kids in today's  world named after harry potter and game  of thrones characters but when it comes  to naming kids after thundercats  characters lino seems more appropriate  for a pet cat than a human  nonetheless that didn't stop several  moms and dads of the 80s from naming  their kids after their favorite  thundercat  i  am chitara  in my heart i know i'm the strongest of  my kind  according to the baby name blog nancy's  baby names seven baby girls were named  chitara after the character debuted in  1985. in 1986 36 baby girls were also  named after chitara with 29 more girls  named in 1987 and an additional nine  baby chitaros in 1988. there's currently  no information for 1989 suggesting  that's where the trend may have ended  however that still leaves 81 people  named after jitara in the united states  now that's wild  despite a promising start the 2011  reboot of thundercats had its life cut  short on cartoon network a variety of  factors worked against the new series  with the most significant disadvantage  being that its toy line wasn't selling  enough for its parent company bandai as  acknowledged by series art director dan  norton it's a shame as the new  thundercats had ambitious plans for its  second season one of which would have  been an episode dedicated entirely to  chitara according to a 2017 interview  norton claimed that the fourth episode  of season two would have focused on  chitara and her status as the last  cleric of thundera the audience would  have also been introduced to an old  rival of chitara described as a snow  leopard the episode would have also  revealed that chitara blames herself for  her grandma's death as she wasn't fast  enough to deliver medicine for her when  she forgave herself the weights that  chitara had been wearing would break  chitara would also gain the ability to  see into the future in this episode just  like in her original incarnation  even the most casual of fans will  remember most of the original characters  from the 1985 thundercats cartoons the  second season however introduced three  new feline characters to the thundercats  crew pamyra linxo and bengali resembling  an alternate color tigra bengali is the  blacksmith of the crew specializing in  forging and repairing weapons most  notably he fixes lino's sword of omens  after it gets snapped in two in the 2011  reboot pumira is introduced in season  one and if the show had lived on bengali  would have appeared as well according to  an interview with dan norton bengali  would have appeared as the son of  chitara and tigra given how similar  tigra and bengali look in the original  series one would assume that making  bengali tigra's son was a way for the  2011 crew to explain their extreme  similarities  [Music]  you

